Patch 2056: every fragment program is decompiled through the buffered path and reads its constants from fp_k[] in
the per-draw b1 slot, which render_frame already fills from the draw's own ucode (FP_KBUF=0 off).

The plain decompile baked constants into the shader as literals, while the pipeline key (fpm_hash) leaves them out.
A program shared by several draws kept the first draw's values, and the shader text changed with every value (the
unused lanes hold leftover bytes), so shader_cache.bin never stopped growing and fights compiled shaders every few
seconds. Programs with more than 64 constants keep the literal path.

Tested (US disc, bench.ps1 quick Free Battle route, HITCH=50): shader cache misses per Free Battle 557 / 585 / 81 /
108 over four runs (before: 300-1200 each run, never settling); 100-400 ms hitches 38 / 17 / 21 / 22 (before ~35-48);
Free Battle 28.5-29.5 flips/s, demo 27.8 / 28.2. Pictures: the dojo floor has more contrast, reflections and shadows;
reviewed by eye: the look improves, character shadows look a bit off (to fix later) (bench/exp/2026-11-08_1203-kbuf1 .. 1244-kbuf4).

